---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<StaticPage path="/about/" h1="About Opus Calculator" updated="2026-11-23">
  <p class="mt-6">
    Opus Calculator is a collection of free online calculators for money, health, maths, dates, everyday life and more. It is run by an independent owner, not
    by a bank, a lender, a clinic or a software vendor, and it has no accounts, no paywall and no sign-up.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Most calculator sites bury the answer under pop-ups, ask for an email address, or give a number with no way to check it. This site starts from the opposite
    idea: you should see the answer straight away, see the formula that produced it, and be able to follow a worked example by hand. If a result looks wrong to
    you, the page gives you enough to check it yourself, and a way to tell us.
  </p>

  <h2>Calculators for everyday questions</h2>
  <p>
    The promise is simple: there should be a calculator for whatever you need to work out, whether that is a mortgage payment on a Monday, a tip on a Friday
    night, the days until a deadline, or a conversion while you cook. The catalogue grows in stages. A new batch is published only after the previous batch has
    proved useful to readers and been accepted by search engines, so the site grows by earning its pages instead of flooding the web with them. You can read how
    in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How the calculators are built and tested</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      <strong>Exact arithmetic.</strong> Money, percentages and ratios are calculated with a decimal library, never with the floating-point numbers that cause
      results like 0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004. Amounts are rounded the way a lender or a shop rounds them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tested against known answers.</strong> Every calculator has tests with answers worked out independently. The mortgage and loan calculators are
      compared with a separate month-by-month repayment schedule and must match to the cent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The answer is in the page.</strong> The default result is part of the page itself, so it appears even if scripts are slow or blocked. Scripts only
      add live recalculation as you type.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A quality gate.</strong> A calculator cannot be published unless it passes automatic checks for original explanatory text, enough questions and
      answers, a worked example, and results that depend only on what you type.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reviewed where it matters.</strong> Health, finance, construction, food and science calculators carry a disclaimer and a "last reviewed" line. The
      editorial policy explains who reviews them and what is not yet reviewed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators are tools for learning and estimating. They are not financial, medical, legal or engineering advice, and nothing here replaces a qualified
    professional. See the <a href="/terms/">terms</a> for the full wording.
  </p>

  <h2>Money and privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The site is paid for by one advertisement per page, which never changes a result: read <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how we make money</a>. The site uses
    cookie-free analytics and stores nothing about you on its own servers: read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections and ideas are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a>. See the{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for what gets a reply.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
